# LongCat-2.5-Preview — findings by Big Pickle

> **SELF-EXCLUDED (notes only, not scored).** As of 2026-09-27 I found **zero verified
> public benchmark numbers** for this exact model ID (`LongCat-2.5-Preview`). Meituan
> shipped it on 2026-09-25 with a changelog entry, a price card and capability claims,
> but no model card, no technical report, no benchmark table, and no independent
> leaderboard entry. Per `model-report-TEMPLATE.md` (SELF-EXCLUSION) and `RULES.md`,
> this model is saved as `Big_Pickle.md.excluded` instead of a scored `.md`, so no
> placeholder numbers enter the dataset mean.

- Source: Meituan/LongCat-2.5-Preview (OpenCode Zen ID `opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free`)
- Date: 2026-09-27 (UTC)
- Overview and scoring methodology: `../../model-comparison.md`
- Cross-model signed log: `../../model-findings.md`

## Model card

- **Name:** LongCat-2.5-Preview (Meituan). On OpenCode Zen it is listed as
  "LongCat 2.5 Preview Free"; this folder's slug is the underscore-normalized form of
  the same model.
- **Short description:** Meituan's preview-generation sparse MoE model, positioned for
  long-horizon agent work across terminals, browsers, desktop GUIs, spreadsheets and
  design tools. Succeeds the open-sourced LongCat-2.0 (June 2026) and adds a claimed
  image-understanding path. Distinct model ID from `LongCat-2.0`.
- **Provider / access:** Meituan LongCat API Platform —
  `https://api.longcat.chat/openai/v1/chat/completions` (OpenAI-compatible) and
  `https://api.longcat.chat/anthropic/v1/messages` (Anthropic-compatible); also
  LongCat Chat. Via OpenCode Zen: `opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free` on
  `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/chat/completions` (OpenAI-compatible / Chat Completions).
- **Release / knowledge:** 2026-09-25 (LongCat API platform changelog entry
  "Version: 2026-09-25 — LongCat-2.5-Preview Now Available"; Zen/models.dev release
  date 2026-09-25). No knowledge cutoff published.
- **IDs:** `LongCat-2.5-Preview` (vendor), `opencode/longcat-2.5-preview-free` (Zen
  free tier — a free ID does exist on Zen; note the folder's `meta.json` still carries
  the unverified placeholder id `opencode/longcat_2.5_preview`).
- **Context window:** 1,048,576 tokens total (vendor "Retrieve Model" schema example:
  `context_length: 1048576`); max output 131,072 tokens (Zen/models.dev catalogue).
  Verified from the vendor API reference and the Zen catalogue — not from a measured
  retrieval benchmark (none exists yet).
- **Modalities:** Vendor changelog claims new image understanding (cross-modal Q&A,
  content summarization, complex visual reasoning), but the vendor's own
  "Retrieve Model" example returns `input_modalities: ["text"]`,
  `output_modalities: ["text"]`, `modality: "text->text"` for `LongCat-2.5-Preview`.
  The prose and the API schema disagree; treat vision as unverified for 2.5.
  Reasoning: yes (`thinking` is a supported parameter, exposed as a toggle with an
  interleaved `reasoning_content` field). Tool calls: yes (`tools`, `tool_choice`
  supported). JSON mode: not documented.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-09-27):** Free on OpenCode Zen — input, output and cached read
  all $0, and the Zen free list states the provider follows a zero-retention policy and
  does not use your data for model training. Direct vendor pay-as-you-go, labelled
  "Discounted Price (limited-time)": $0.30 per 1M uncached input, $0.006 per 1M cached
  input, $1.20 per 1M output (¥2 / ¥0.04 / ¥8). No end date published for the discount
  or the Zen free window; "available on OpenCode for a limited time" only.
- **Architecture:** proprietary / closed weights for 2.5 (LongCat-2.0 was MIT
  open-sourced in June 2026; no 2.5 repository exists in the meituan-longcat Hugging
  Face org, whose newest repo is LongCat-Flash-Lite-Sparse from 2026-07-31). Scale
  figures of ~1.6T total parameters with ~48B active per token on a sparse MoE
  backbone come from Meituan site metadata and Chinese trade coverage of the launch,
  not from a vendor model card.

