Long context:

- no long-context retrieval reported — the 1M window is a spec, not a measured
  RULER / MRCR / GraphWalks result. No recall number exists for this model.

Search coverage used (2026-09-27): LongCat API docs pricing page, LongCat changelog,
LongCat "Retrieve Model" API reference, OpenCode Zen docs (model + pricing + privacy
tables), and dated launch coverage from orcarouter.ai, eyestech.in, cocoloop and a
Japanese technical write-up. All four independent write-ups state explicitly that no
vendor or third-party benchmark exists for 2.5 and that any circulating "LongCat-2.5"
score is either another LongCat model or invented.

### Closest available reference — DIFFERENT MODEL, NOT SCORED, NOT A PROXY CLAIM

LongCat-2.0 (open-sourced 2026-06, MIT) has an in-house evaluation table on
`github.com/meituan-longcat/LongCat-2.0`: Terminal-Bench 2.1 70.8, SWE-bench Pro 59.5,
SWE-bench Multilingual 77.3, FORTE 73.2, BrowseComp 79.9, RWSearch 78.8, IFEval 90.0,
Writing Bench 83.8, IMO-AnswerBench 81.8, GPQA-diamond 88.9. These are **2.0** numbers
under Meituan's unified in-house harness (competitor figures marked `*` are cited from
the competitor's own report). They describe a different model ID and are recorded here
only so a later revision does not re-derive them; they are provisional for 2.5 and are
explicitly **not** used as a stand-in for it.

## Normalized scores (1–100)

Not scored. Self-excluded: the `Overall Score` needs the mean of the five quality
dims, and every one of those dims would rest on invented numbers. Nothing is written
here on purpose — the free Zen window is the only honest way to produce a real table
for this model.

